claimed: script-config -- okay-script's seventeen OKAY_* variables as ONE
Schema'd config, and the layering that reads it (BACKLOG, stage 0's
remainder).

okay-conf gains the layering every config in this repo will want:
defaults -> file -> environment, by RFC 7396 merge over the value's own
JSON, with Conf.envName as the ONE derivation of an environment name
from a field (okay-deploy's Settings.envName delegates to it, so the
name is derived in one place rather than agreed in two). A value the
environment cannot supply is a refusal naming the variable, never a
silent default.

okay-script's Serve.Config is that case class; Args is built from it,
so the pair refusals (cert without key, acme without domains) stay
where they are. ScriptDeploy derives the deployment's settings from
the same value, which is the whole point: the names in the unit file
and the names the process reads are one list.

Files: okay-conf/src/main/scala/okay/conf/Conf.scala, okay-deploy
Deployment.scala, okay-script Serve.scala + ScriptDeploy.scala, tests,
specs/conf.md + specs/okay-script.md, boards.
